  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "14466322",
      "title": "The Anatomy of a Http Request",
      "lectureOrder": 578,
      "videoOrder": 531,
      "sourceHash": "88685ba0f3e7029c663492b8c7ab1e75b05dda8dd81cd92a898ba54b24811428",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.22,
          "end": 4.23,
          "en": "-: Before we start sending requests",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.23,
          "end": 8.37,
          "en": "it's important to understand the anatomy of an Http request",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 8.37,
          "end": 12.57,
          "en": "because an Http request is made up of a couple of core parts",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 12.57,
          "end": 13.92,
          "en": "which we'll all have a look at",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 13.92,
          "end": 15.84,
          "en": "in this module here when it comes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 15.84,
          "end": 18.69,
          "en": "to configuring them when sending a request.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 18.69,
          "end": 21.78,
          "en": "The most important part about a request, of course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 21.78,
          "end": 24.42,
          "en": "is the URL you are sending the request to.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 24.42,
          "end": 27,
          "en": "That's also called the API Endpoint",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 27,
          "end": 31.29,
          "en": "and it is something like your domain.com/post/one.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 31.29,
          "end": 32.31,
          "en": "For example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 32.31,
          "end": 34.26,
          "en": "The exact path here, of course",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 34.26,
          "end": 37.26,
          "en": "depends on the API you are interacting with.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 37.26,
          "end": 40.11,
          "en": "However, when communicating with a restful API",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 40.11,
          "end": 41.88,
          "en": "it's not just about the URL,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 41.88,
          "end": 44.61,
          "en": "but also about the Http word you're using",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 44.61,
          "end": 46.89,
          "en": "something like POST, GET, PUT.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 46.89,
          "end": 49.68,
          "en": "This defines which kind of request you wanna send",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 49.68,
          "end": 50.85,
          "en": "to that endpoint.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 50.85,
          "end": 52.56,
          "en": "Do you want to store new data?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 52.56,
          "end": 53.91,
          "en": "Do you want to fetch data?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 53.91,
          "end": 55.98,
          "en": "Do you want to replace existing data?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 55.98,
          "end": 59.31,
          "en": "The Http word makes that clear, but it always depends",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 59.31,
          "end": 61.98,
          "en": "on the API you're working with, which endpoints,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 61.98,
          "end": 64.68,
          "en": "and which words for these endpoints are available.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 64.68,
          "end": 68.01,
          "en": "So the official docs for the API is always the place to go",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 68.01,
          "end": 70.28999999999999,
          "en": "unless you're of course writing your own API",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 70.28999999999999,
          "end": 71.7,
          "en": "in which case, you of course know",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 71.7,
          "end": 74.103,
          "en": "which endpoint supports which operations.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 75.03,
          "end": 76.59,
          "en": "Now, when we're sending a request",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 76.59,
          "end": 79.402,
          "en": "it's nice to know where and how to send it to that place",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 79.402,
          "end": 83.01,
          "en": "but you often also need to set additional metadata.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 83.01,
          "end": 85.5,
          "en": "The so-called headers of a request.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 85.5,
          "end": 88.77,
          "en": "Now, these are kind of optional or to be precise.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 88.77,
          "end": 90.63,
          "en": "Some default headers will be appended",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 90.63,
          "end": 94.11,
          "en": "to a request for you by the browser and by Angular",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 94.11,
          "end": 96.24000000000001,
          "en": "but you can also append your own headers",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 96.24000000000001,
          "end": 98.07,
          "en": "and that is there for (indistinct)something",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 98.07,
          "end": 99.78,
          "en": "we'll have a look at.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 99.78,
          "end": 104.13,
          "en": "Now, last but not least, for some Http words",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 104.13,
          "end": 106.86,
          "en": "you can also add a body to your request.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 106.86,
          "end": 109.53,
          "en": "That's the core data that is attached to a request.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 109.53,
          "end": 110.363,
          "en": "For example",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 110.363,
          "end": 113.75999999999999,
          "en": "if you are sending a post request to create a new piece",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 113.75999999999999,
          "end": 116.00999999999999,
          "en": "of data on the server, well, then of course",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 116.00999999999999,
          "end": 118.97999999999999,
          "en": "you should attach the information about that piece of data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 118.97999999999999,
          "end": 122.31,
          "en": "to your request, and you would do that in the request body.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 122.31,
          "end": 124.38,
          "en": "Therefore, a request body can be set",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 124.38,
          "end": 127.47,
          "en": "on POST, PUT, and PATCH requests, which are requests",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 127.47,
          "end": 132.36,
          "en": "that you alter data on the server by adding or replacing it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 132.36,
          "end": 135.21,
          "en": "Now, that's the general anatomy of an Http request.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 135.21,
          "end": 138.96,
          "en": "Let's now have a look at how Angular helps us with writing",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 138.96,
          "end": 142.02,
          "en": "or with creating such requests, how we can work with them,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 142.02,
          "end": 143.52,
          "en": "how we can work with the response",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 143.52,
          "end": 145.53300000000002,
          "en": "and what else Angular has to offer.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
